			<div class="content" id="post-content-4804042">
									

<p>Requested trade.</p>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">「Line&nbsp;by&nbsp;Line」</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">「Close」</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is an abnormally short saguaro cactus1 (approximately 2 meters) with two arms.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The footnote isn't entirely needed and can be combined. Additionally, there's a bit of inconsistency. You use [2 meters] then switch to [two arms], two is written differently in the same sentence. &gt; [SCP-XXXX is an abnormally large saguaro cactus (<em>Carnegiea gigantiea</em>) at approximately two meters with two arms.]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is planted in an orange ceramic pot and it is always seen hovering .3 meters above the floor.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Could probably cut down a bit: [It is planted in an orange ceramic pot, hovering 0.3 meters above the floor.]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It has an accent that varies between individuals who hear it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Describe the accents. What accents do people hear? European? Canadian? Californian?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While its method of communication is predominantly telepathic, voice recording technology is capable of recording a corrupted version of its speech. (See addenda.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Combine the brackets. [of its speech (See Addendum XXXX-1 or -2, specify).]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX's anomalous properties include</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A cactus being sentient and can talk via telepathy is already anomalous. Maybe reword this to fit [Other anomalous qualities.]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>bullets with a trajectory that is not affected by wind</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I suggest: [bullets with a trajectory unaffected by wind.]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Reports of a talking cactus in the Chihuahuan Desert in the state of Texas had brought the possibility of anomalous activity to the Foundation's attention.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It feels like you're missing something here. I suggest adding [SCP-XXXX was discovered when-].</p>
<blockquote>
<p>See addendum.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Brackets.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Field agents Egrene and Philips arrive at Chihuahuan Desert. Thick plumes of sand dirt are thrown into the air as SCP-XXXX hurtles through the blizzard.&gt;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missed formatting at the beginning. Also, add a [the] before Chihuahuan.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>field agents.&quot;&gt;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You have a quote here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>in the soil&gt;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missed a period.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX: Where are you, you no good, job-stealing crow toilet?!<br />
&lt;Explosions sporadically occur within a 15 meter radius of SCP-XXXX's gunfire.&gt;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You missed a paragraph break here. I also suggest adding a dash between [15] and [meter.]</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Stop There's no need for that!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe add a comma after [Stop], or a exclamation mark. Anything that signals a short break, since the next word is capitalized, and makes it flow better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Egrene: Th-thank you…</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels a bit stilted. Maybe something like [Thanks&#8230;?] would work better.</p>
<hr />
<p>As a sidenote, even if it sort of makes sense in-universe to keep records of an untranslated version, I don't see what it adds to this? It feels like it's there to take up space, and if it's not essential to the narrative, I suggest you just cut it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">「Overall」</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">「Close」</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Overall, it's not bad. It knows what it does, and gets that job done well. I think the initial encounter could be improved a bit. I can tell you were trying to go for a more satirical vibe, but that just didn't click with me. Or I could just be unfunny. That aside, I think alright in its current state. I don't feel like you need to add anything or such. It's a short, self-contained narrative. Just spice up the humour, and I think you'll be on your way.</p>
<p>Because in its current state, I'd probably just leave it to a no-vote because the humor didn't land, and sort of killed it for me.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

