<p>Hello! I am here per our IRC exchange to offer crit</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Crit&nbsp;lives&nbsp;within</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Yeeted&nbsp;and&nbsp;Deleeted</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<h3><span>ConProcs</span></h3>
<blockquote>
<p>The temperature in its containment chamber is to be kept at a minimum of 28 degrees Celsius.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would indicate which direction this errs. Is higher okay? Or is lower?</p>
<p>This is an otherwise very brief section so I have little to say. We just get right on into it and I'm good with that.</p>
<p>+++Description</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Two arms extend from the central portion of its body.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Consider: &quot;Two arms extend from center mass&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>via levitation, usually at most 0.3 meters above the ground.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Language cleanup and significant digits. Consider: &quot;levitation at an elevation of approximately 30cm&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is sentient and capable of speech via telepathy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You might mean sapient. You might also want to say &quot;communication via telepathy&quot; rather than speech.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>recording a corrupted version of its speech.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;corrupted version&quot; is highly dubious.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is capable of firing regular revolver ammunition</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since we just switched to the -1 I think it's probably fine, but, you could maybe stand to clarify the noun here a bit better in this passage.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>bullets with a trajectory unaffected by wind,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wind is only a factor at distances which are pretty well in excess of the range of a revolver.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It then traveled 6 kilometers across the city of Hollister,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I want to bring this up because the entire rest of this article is just one massive masquerade breach and you never cover or refer to that explicitly. There are &quot;sightings&quot; and nobody seems to call out the fact a levitating cactus is talking to them as it fights crime. If you want people to be nonplussed that is certainly an approach you can take, but we, as the Foundation, categorically should not be abiding this as &quot;business as usual&quot;.</p>
<h3><span>Video Logs</span></h3>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX 'kicks' open the front door to a Starbucks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This factually can't happen so I don't get why we're being coy. The door explodes inward, or, the door opens unassisted. This isn't very clinical even though I know exactly what you mean.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>evaded capture for approximately 8 hours</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This kind of begs the question of escalation. Why are we letting some random embedded agents chase this guy for a full day without sending help? Reduce the number, or send help.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>technicians who smelled gunpowder in the water supply</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't follow what this is implying and it never seems to come up again. You also probably wouldn't &quot;smell&quot; gunpowder; it only has a distinct smell when it's been fired/spent and that's not going to happen in water.</p>
<p>I liked the characterization of the video logs overall but I do have to warn you about your dialogue; you use a truly stupendous amount of exclamation points, and when they are so common they lose their meaning. Please strongly reconsider how you are applying this punctuation with an aim toward toning it down.</p>
<p>The best place to use an exclamation is after an interjection or command word. This is a way to suddenly or notably raise the level of emotion so you want to apply it rarely so people notice the departure from baseline. If every other line has an exclamation then that is a very excited and exhausting new baseline. I can clarify further if you want.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I would like to read this again to offer more thoughts as you explore the issues with the town, or alternatively, tighten up the timeline so those issues can be brushed away. As it stands, I am having trouble getting into what you're presenting because of the issues with the framework. I will say, in general, the central character does convey a good sense of identity but I think that their perseverance in the face of a less accommodating world might make them come through even more.</p>

